<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Tarhuntassa</h1><p class="st-meta">1280 BCE – 1180 BCE (approx.) · capital Tarhuntassa</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Tarhuntassa, a Hittite royal city and later a rival appanage kingdom, whose rulers challenged the great kings at Hattusa.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1280 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muwatalli-ii">Muwatalli II</a> moved the Hittite capital, with the gods of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a>, to Tarhuntassa, a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> whose site is still unknown. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/urhi-teshub">Urhi-Teshub</a> moved the court back, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusili-iii">Hattusili III</a> made Tarhuntassa an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/appanage">appanage</a> kingdom for Muwatalli's other son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurunta">Kurunta</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Tarhuntassa ruled the Lower Land towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> as a high-ranking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. A treaty between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tudhaliya-iv">Tudhaliya IV</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurunta">Kurunta</a>, on a bronze tablet found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> in 1986, defines its borders and privileges. Seals suggest Kurunta later claimed the title great king.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Rivalry between Tarhuntassa and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusa">Hattusa</a> weakened the empire in its last decades. Both collapsed c. 1180 BCE; afterwards a great king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hartapu">Hartapu</a>, known from inscriptions at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kizildag">Kızıldağ</a>, ruled in the region.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/tarhuntassa.jpg" alt="Tarhuntassa" width="320" height="427"><figcaption>Image: Bjørn Christian Tørrissen · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hattusa_Bronze_Tablet_Cuneiform.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1280 BCE – 1180 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century-bce">13th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tarhuntassa</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muwatalli II, Kurunta, Ulmi-Teshub</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hittite religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hittite, Luwian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Tarhuntassa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1230&amp;focus=tarhuntassa" aria-label="Tarhuntassa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5512 849 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Tarhuntassa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5832 1105L5852 1002"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5852 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5832 1105h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5832 1105h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-1230&amp;focus=tarhuntassa">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

